From 2750ce1781f627e0931f2693ee7a213cc0705343 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:32:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: open an input that FFmpeg reads itself only once

CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::Open() opened a stream that FFmpeg reads itself
(DVDSTREAM_TYPE_FFMPEG: HLS, UDP and RTP, RTSP, RTMP, the second mms
attempt), closed it, and opened it again with load_all_variants=0. In
2019 the first call only probed (AVFMT_FLAG_PRIV_OPT) and the second
read the header with the HLS option set; a fix for a leaked context made
it a close and a whole second open, and the option came from the FFmpeg
that Kodi used to carry patches in. No FFmpeg that Kodi builds with now
has it: no source file of the 9.0.2 that the image builds (with the
patches of LibreELEC and Hades) names it, nor do Kodi's own depends. So
every such stream was connected to and probed twice, every playlist of
an HLS stream loaded twice and a multicast group joined twice, to make
the same context. The YBLOD fork measured about 1.5 s per change of a
live channel (not measured here).

It is opened once, with the option still passed, where an FFmpeg might
take it; one that does not leaves it in the dictionary, which is freed
as before. The second open also gave a context with the interrupt
callback to the mmst attempt that follows a failed mmsh one (that
failure frees the context, and avformat_open_input() makes one without
it): the open makes that context itself now.

Host test (demux_open_test.cpp, against FFmpeg 9.0.2 built for the host
with its HLS and MPEG-TS demuxers): no demuxer, protocol or context has
the option; an open with it leaves it in the dictionary and opens
exactly what an open without it opens, five inputs for a master
playlist of two variants and one for a transport stream; the open,
close and open of before opened each of them twice.

Idea from the YBLOD fork, 00afece129; rewritten (it kept the first open
for live MPEG-TS only).
---
 .../DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp            | 25 ++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
index 564f90b..9d0cb41 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -358,22 +358,23 @@ bool CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::Open(const std::shared_ptr<CDVDInputStream>& pInput, bool
     }
     if (result < 0)
     {
-      if (avformat_open_input(&m_pFormatContext, strFile.c_str(), iformat, &options) < 0)
+      // Hades: opened once. It was opened, closed, and opened again with load_all_variants=0, an
+      // option of the HLS demuxer of the FFmpeg that Kodi used to carry patches in, which no FFmpeg
+      // it builds with now has (9.0.2 has no option of that name anywhere): every stream was
+      // connected to and probed twice, and every playlist of an HLS stream loaded twice, for the
+      // same context. The option still goes with the open, where an FFmpeg might take it; one that
+      // does not leaves it in the dictionary.
+      av_dict_set_int(&options, "load_all_variants", 0, 0);
+      // a failed attempt (mmsh, above) freed the context, and the one avformat_open_input() would
+      // make has no interrupt callback (the second open gave it one)
+      if (!m_pFormatContext)
       {
-        CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "Error, could not open file {}", CURL::GetRedacted(strFile));
-        Dispose();
-        av_dict_free(&options);
-        return false;
+        m_pFormatContext = avformat_alloc_context();
+        m_pFormatContext->interrupt_callback = int_cb;
       }
-      av_dict_free(&options);
-      avformat_close_input(&m_pFormatContext);
-      m_pFormatContext = avformat_alloc_context();
-      m_pFormatContext->interrupt_callback = int_cb;
-      AVDictionary* options = GetFFMpegOptionsFromInput();
-      av_dict_set_int(&options, "load_all_variants", 0, AV_OPT_SEARCH_CHILDREN);
       if (avformat_open_input(&m_pFormatContext, strFile.c_str(), iformat, &options) < 0)
       {
-        CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "Error, could not open file (2) {}", CURL::GetRedacted(strFile));
+        CLog::Log(LOGDEBUG, "Error, could not open file {}", CURL::GetRedacted(strFile));
         Dispose();
         av_dict_free(&options);
         return false;
-- 
